},{},{},{},{},{},{},{},{},{},{},{},{},{},{},{},{},{},{},{},{},{},{},{},{},{},{},{},{},{},{},{},{},{},{},{},{},{},{},{},{},{},{},{},{},{},{},{},{}],"verses":["13:1","13:2","13:3","13:4","13:5","13:6","13:7","13:8","13:9"],"en":{"13:1":"At that time some of those present told Jesus about the Galileans whose blood Pilate had mixed with their sacrifices.","13:2":"To this He replied, “Do you think that these Galileans were worse sinners than all the other Galileans, because they suffered this way?","13:3":"No, I tell you. But unless you repent, you too will all perish.","13:4":"Or those eighteen who were killed when the tower of Siloam collapsed on them: Do you think that they were more sinful than all the others living in Jerusalem?","13:5":"No, I tell you. But unless you repent, you too will all perish.”","13:6":"Then Jesus told this parable: “A man had a fig tree that was planted in his vineyard. He went to look for fruit on it but did not find any.","13:7":"So he said to the keeper of the vineyard, ‘Look, for the past three years I have come to search for fruit on this fig tree and haven’t found any. Therefore cut it down! Why should it use up the soil?’","13:8":"‘Sir,’ the man replied, ‘leave it alone again this year, until I dig around it and fertilize it.","13:9":"If it bears fruit next year, fine. But if not, you can cut it down.’”"}}},"pairs":{},"minor":[]}